## Fix: design-gaps review
================================================================================

Context: The review of the design-traceability round found no Critical and five
Important findings: the source-overwrite check could be skipped (its versions came
from the store base, which a scheduled tick ends), lost (a failed full refresh
recorded no versions; versions were read after the update) or bypassed by the tick;
several rewrites went undetected and the history read was unbounded; the external
EXPLAIN check never ran in CI; the drift remedy was incomplete (a MERGE build
cleared it, batch-only domains were never reconciled, `_data` was not recomputed);
and the status endpoint probed everything for `full` domains on every page load.
Plus minors on the UI, the preflight, the gates, the facts, the tick and the
property test.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py (`mappings_for`),
   TwinIncrementalReadiness.py, TwinSlotReconciliation.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py (7b77cd54)
   One mapping derivation for the readiness preflight, the reconciliation and the
   scheduled tick. The tick's base URI default was `http://example.org/` where the
   build's is `DEFAULT_BASE_URI`; a domain without an ontology base URI now gets
   the same mappings on both paths.
2. src/back/core/streaming/SourceReadiness.py (1d46d2d1)
   I2: `CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE`, `REPLACE TABLE`, `CLONE` / `SHALLOW CLONE` /
   `DEEP CLONE` and a `Complete`-mode `STREAMING UPDATE` count as rewrites;
   `DESCRIBE HISTORY` is limited to the versions since the recorded one; a newest
   version below it (DROP + CREATE) is a rewrite; no new version reads nothing; a
   window above 10000 versions counts as a rewrite.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinSlotRefreshPlan.py (new, re-exported),
   TwinBuildRunHistory.py, TwinIncrementalBuild.py, TwinScheduledRefresh.py,
   _build_pipeline.py, src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py (deea846e)
   I1 + I4a + I4c: every slot update — a build's and an incremental tick's — is
   planned by `TwinSlotRefreshPlan`: a full refresh when a source was rewritten
   (another table id, a restarted history, a rewrite in its history) since the
   versions the last completed update recorded (the newest run that has them, not
   the store base), or while one is owed. Versions and table ids are read before
   the update and recorded only once it and the `_data` refresh completed;
   `slot_full_refresh_pending` stays true until then and a run whose update did
   not complete carries the previous versions forward, so the next build or tick
   retries. A drift owes a full slot refresh and `REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW … FULL`
   (batch-only domains: the view refresh); MERGE and full builds record no slot
   facts and pass the debt on. `slot_full_refresh_reason` replaces overwriting
   `mode_fallback_reason` with `source_overwritten`. The tick records the same
   facts (attached to its run's stats before the update, so a failed tick leaves
   the refresh pending) and rebuilds by CTAS when a source history is unreadable.
   `TwinBuildRunHistory.recent_runs` reads the 50-run window once per build;
   `reconcile_drift_pending` is gone. TwinIncrementalBuild 401 -> 374 lines.
4. src/back/core/streaming/SlotReconciler.py, TwinSlotReconciliation.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py, src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   (0dfff0fb)
   I4b + minors: a domain without `_slots` compares the gateway VIEW and the synced
   table alone (`slots_present: false`; 404 only with nothing to compare); the
   on-demand VIEW scan is opt-in (`?recompute=true`), the tick always runs it; the
   tick no longer reconciles `microbatch` domains, counts the synced table only when
   its refresh came `ONLINE`, and catches any exception.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalStatus.py,
   TwinIncrementalReadiness.py, src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   (b96ec2ab)
   I5: a `full` domain's status is answered without any warehouse, pipelines or
   registry call. The preflight reports the MERGE promotion (`merge_fallback`,
   `TwinMergeFallback.promotes`) and mappings that do not compile (`compile_error`,
   the build's `incremental_failed:ValidationError`) instead of a bare 400; the
   enable action checks `resp.ok`. The gate tests assert `ROLE_BUILDER` on every
   incremental route; the docs say builders.
6. tests/external/test_mv_incremental_plan.py, .github/workflows/nightly.yml
   (a06bccf6)
   I3: the external EXPLAIN check also takes `DATABRICKS_HOST` /
   `DATABRICKS_TOKEN` / `DATABRICKS_SQL_WAREHOUSE_ID` (the nightly
   `external-smoke` credentials) and creates its schema; the job sets
   `ONTOBRICKS_EXTERNAL_WAREHOUSE=1` and `ONTOBRICKS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA` (repository
   variable `ONTOBRICKS_INT_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA`, default `main.ontobricks_it`).
7. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py,
   tests/property/test_slot_fold.py (moved from tests/units/streaming/) (4449e07e)
   Deletes rank 0 like pre-images (`CASE WHEN _change_type IN
   ('update_preimage','delete') THEN 0 ELSE 1 END AS seq_rank`): a key a commit
   deletes and inserts again ends upserted (before, both ranked 1). The property
   test generates such replaces and NULL-key rows. The new slot SQL changes the
   pipeline fingerprint: the next build of each incremental domain runs one full
   refresh, and ticks rebuild `_data` by CTAS until that build.
8. docs/incremental-materialization.md
   The full-refresh rules (sticky, before/after versions, table ids, the bounded
   history), the trace-key table (`source_versions`, `source_table_ids`,
   `slot_full_refresh_pending`, `slot_full_refresh_reason`, `reconcile_drift`),
   reconciliation without slots and the opt-in recompute, the tick rules, the
   status early return, the preflight fields, the slot ordering, and both
   credential paths of the Verification section.

Known limitations (follow-ups):
- Live-unverified as before: EXPLAIN output, `information_schema` table types,
  `DESCRIBE HISTORY` / `DESCRIBE DETAIL` on MVs and streaming tables, and the
  `CLONE` / `STREAMING UPDATE` operation names and their `outputMode` parameter.
- A source with more than 10000 commits between two slot updates is fully
  refreshed every time (conservative; the change feed itself would still work).
- The nightly schema default `main.ontobricks_it` must exist or be creatable by
  the integration token; otherwise set the repository variable.

