## Fix: Phase 3 re-review
================================================================================

Context: Re-review of the Phase 3 review fixes: three items still open
(development-mode pipeline names after a bind, envelope errors that still
crashed the stream, and a gap between the _live seed and the stream's start)
plus minors. B's core files are untouched.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SlotPipelineRunner.py (C4)
   `find_pipeline` matches `<name>` and the development-mode `[dev <user>]
   <name>` (an exact name wins; two distinct candidates raise ConflictError)
   and backs `find_pipeline_id`, the fingerprint and bundle-managed reads;
   `ensure` keeps the deployed name when it updates a prefixed pipeline.
2. databricks.yml, scripts/_internal/_ensure-instance-target.sh,
   scripts/_internal/_render-slot-pipelines.py (C4)
   The development targets (dev, dev-lakebase, generated dev-lakebase-<id>)
   set `presets: {name_prefix: "", pipelines_development: false}`; the
   renderer prints a notice when a deployed pipeline still carries a prefix.
3. scripts/deploy.sh (minor)
   The bind step runs on Lakebase targets only, like the render, and each CLI
   call reads /dev/null instead of the bind list.
4. src/jobs/triple_stream/TripleStreamEnvelope.py (I9)
   explode_records skips and counts any ValueError, TypeError,
   ArithmeticError (OverflowError, decimal.InvalidOperation) or
   ValidationError per envelope, with a %-style warning naming the type.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinLiveServing.py,
   src/jobs/triple_stream/main.py, resources/triple_rtm.job.yml (NEW-1)
   _live is seeded from `_slots VERSION AS OF` its newest version (DESCRIBE
   HISTORY LIMIT 1); the job reads its initial state at the same version
   (`--slots-version`) and replays the topic from that commit's time less a
   10-minute margin (`--start-timestamp-ms`: Kafka / Event Hubs Kafka endpoint
   `startingTimestamp` + `startingOffsetsByTimestampStrategy=latest`, Kinesis
   `initialPosition` `at_timestamp`), so no change between the seed and the
   start is lost.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinRealtimeStream.py,
   TwinBuildRunHistory.py, _build_pipeline.py (NEW-1, minors)
   The job parameters carry `slots_version` and `start_timestamp_ms`; the
   trace records `slots_seed_version`. Cancelling another version's run
   retires that version's _live; a failed upload or run_now after the seed
   retires _live before raising. after_build makes no Postgres query with
   realtime off and records any error as best-effort.
7. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/SyncedTableName.py (new), TwinLiveServing.py (minor)
   refresh_view passes `synced_phy_override` when the synced table is
   registered under a ghost-state fallback name, as the build does.
8. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinSlotReconciliation.py (minor)
   _live is counted only while served: a retired one reports no live_drift.
9. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js, _domain_information.html (minor)
   The save keeps the stored state_ttl_hours (rendered on the section).
10. docs/incremental-materialization.md
    Traceability (Serving after the pinned seed, DAB adoption with the presets
    note), development mode, the pinned seed and replay, the reconciliation
    gate, and the live-unverified list (VERSION AS OF on the streaming table,
    timestamp starts, the empty name prefix).
11. tests
    Prefix resolution (prefixed, exact wins, conflict, longer name, update
    keeps the name), renderer prefix notice, presets, bind gating, envelope
    error types, seed version / replay start / Kinesis position / initial
    state SQL, retire on cancel and on failure, after_build gate, refresh_view
    override, SyncedTableName, reconciliation gate, TTL preservation.

